 lines += ['', 'These are deterministic answer/reference-overlap proxies, not independently verified factual correctness, grounding, completeness or citation validity. CRAG provides no independent passage-level qrels/support annotations, so evidence-ranking endpoints remain `NOT_EVALUABLE`.', '', '## Resources and preservation', '', f"- Corrected selector resources are recorded in `04_analysis/html_text_repair_1/V4_REPAIRED_PAIRED_ANALYSIS.json`; full-Jina p50/p95 latency is {next(x for x in analysis['resource'] if x['policy']=='S1_JINA_FULL_VISIBLE_TEXT')['duration_p50_ms']:.3f}/{next(x for x in analysis['resource'] if x['policy']=='S1_JINA_FULL_VISIBLE_TEXT')['duration_p95_ms']:.3f} ms and peak-memory p95 is {next(x for x in analysis['resource'] if x['policy']=='S1_JINA_FULL_VISIBLE_TEXT')['memory_p95_mib']:.1f} MiB.", '- Original raw-HTML E11-V artifacts and its blocker remain immutable; corrected outputs are append-only under `02_selection/html_text_repair_1/`, `03_reader/html_text_repair_1/` and `04_analysis/html_text_repair_1/`.', '- GPU 5/6 model processes were released after the corrected runs; no unrelated process was terminated. Jev/paid calls: 0/0; protected holdout: unopened.', '- The earlier StartLux kernel dependency is present (`causal_conv1d` and FLA imports pass; targeted runtime tests 2/2). The StartLux checkpoint adapter itself is not part of E11-V and was not introduced here.', '', '## Remaining issue', '', 'The representation/OOM issue is solved for the corrected namespace. The scientific limitation on passage-level evidence quality and independently verified factual correctness is not solvable from CRAG’s existing labels; it requires an independently authorized support annotation or adjudication phase.']
